<title>POLAND: Polish cargo freights in Jan-August up 16.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Polish cargo freights in Jan-August up 16.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's national air carrier LOT said on Monday its cargo traffic increased by 16.8 percent to 10,540 tonnes in the first eight months of this year from the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Polskie Linie Lotnicze LOT SA said in a statement that cargo exports were up 11.8 percent while  its revenues from exports jumped 24 percent to $6.3 million in the period while imports rose 19.8 percent.</p>
<p>CARGO TRADE (in kgs) JAN-AUG 96	 JAN-AUG 95     PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>TOTAL TRADE	    10,539,753	 9,024,798	  16.8</p>
<p>chartered flights	  54,886		   0	     -</p>
<p>scheduled flights     9,923,947	 8,570,628	  15.8</p>
<p>trucks			560,920	   454,170	  23.5</p>
<p>TOTAL EXPORTS	   3,777,853	 3,380,038	  11.8</p>
<p>chartered flights	  14,548		   0	     -</p>
<p>scheduled flights     3,206,307	 2,933,902	   9.3</p>
<p>trucks			556,998	   446,136	  24.8</p>
<p>TOTAL IMPORTS	   6,761,900	 5,644,760	  19.8</p>
<p>chartered flights	  40,338		   0	     -</p>
<p>scheduled flights     6,717,640	 5,636,726	  19.2</p>
<p>trucks			  3,922	     8,034	 -48.8</p>
<p>-- Robert Bogdanski +48 22 653 9700</p>
